 (skeleton)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add GET /login-page: pure HTML consumer of existing POST /login API,
  no new auth logic. Renders web/templates/login.html.
- Add get_current_user dependency in web/app.py: thin wrapper around
  the existing web_session_service.validate_session — behavior of
  validate_session is unchanged, auth_service.py and
  web_session_service.py are untouched.
- Auth-gate GET / (home -> dashboard): unauthenticated requests get a
  303 redirect to /login-page. No DB call happens when no session
  cookie is present (validate_session short-circuits on empty token).
- Rename templates/home.html -> templates/dashboard.html; dashboard
  shows the logged-in user's name, session status, and a placeholder
  list of allowed modules derived only from the existing Users.IsAdmin
  flag. Explicitly does NOT query Transaction/Factors/DocHeader or any
  other Legacy financial data.
- tests/_fake_database.py: add fetch_one support for
  'SELECT * FROM Users WHERE ID = ?' (needed to resolve UserRef from
  validate_session into a display name). No other fixture behavior
  changed.
- tests/test_web_dashboard.py: new tests
  test_dashboard_requires_login, test_dashboard_with_valid_session,
  test_logout_invalidates_session.
- No changes to services/auth_service.py, services/web_session_service.py,
  or database/migrations/015_web_sessions.sql. Migration NOT executed
  against any real database. No Legacy financial structures touched.

Full suite: 248 passed (245 previous + 3 new), 0 removed.
